WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.116
Coding Exercise 4 asks for separate pneumonia and
fracture counts for each

00:00:04.142 --> 00:00:09.724
patient using PostgreSQL FILTER The output grain is
one row per

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:15.295
subject ID You need two count expressions and each
one should have

00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:20.937
its own FILTER condition Do not provide the full
solution immediately

00:00:20.964 --> 00:00:26.295
from memory Build one conditional count first then
create the second using

00:00:26.322 --> 00:00:31.830
the same pattern with a different diagnosis Run and
Check and inspect

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:36.934
a patient who has both types of admissions if one
exists If

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.486
you are practicing in pgAdmin copy the query after
it works and

00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:43.460
compare the FILTER version with how you might write
the same logic

00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:44.657
using SUM and CASE
